  "notes": "Site is Squarespace. Photos are recorded as the URLs the pages serve; some file names carry encoded characters exactly as on the page (plus signs and brackets in the Sip & Sail photo names). All the URLs checked returned an image. Logo is the header logo at the 1500 width the site serves; the footer also uses a full colour logo (pilgrim-logo-full-colour-rgb-150mm@72ppi.png). Hero is the aerial photo of Pilgrim from the Private Charters page; the home page itself opens on a native video, so there is no still hero to compare. Videos: the site links no YouTube or Vimeo channel. The home page plays a 20 second muted looping native video hosted on video.squarespace-cdn.com (HLS playlist at https://video.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/680db373dcd8c5395f4ec242/1748577707798-C4P3XCKEMU9UQVV0VXUE/playlist.m3u8, poster image Website+Cover-Cover.jpg). No .mp4 file URL was found, so it is not listed in videos. Left out on purpose: badge and award images (Earthcheck, Best of Queensland, Tripadvisor, Tourism Awards, Master Reef Guide, Sustainable Tourism, Eco Guide); review quote images (Testimonial-*.jpg and simply-magic); the Instagram feed images on the home page (credited to other people); photos with a Salty Dingo copyright in the file name (Samantha 40th, Pilgrim Sailing Salty Dingo 2017) and the Craig Greenhill Saltwater Images race photos on the Pilgrim the Yacht blog page, which are credited to photographers; Facebook export file names on the blog page; the image on the Amphibious Tours page named unsplash-image-zMwxD1cp-Gk.jpg (stock); stock-looking underwater reef and turtle images on the About page; the Maggie Island Brewery producer image (another business); gift shop merchandise photos; the ATE25FP image on the home page (looks like a trade event card); the generic Website Cover-Cover.jpg used as a page header (it is the video poster and may carry text). Trip photos come from each trip page (header image, the four Glimpse photos and the closing photo) plus the card images on the All Experiences page; the three private charter pages share many photos, so Private Day Charter and Private Sunset Charter lists come from their own pages only. The Sandy small boat tours have no live product page (404), so there are no trip photos for them. No bot check, captcha or block was met on pilgrimsailing.com.au."
